meta {
  name: Edit/Resubmit Offline Token Payment (Student)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/payments/courses/token/offline/{{offlineTransactionId}}/resubmit
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "payment_method": "bank_transfer",
    "amount": 25000,
    "proof_url": "https://cdn.example.com/proof/transfer-456.pdf",
    "proof_file_name": "transfer-456.pdf",
    "bank_ref_number": "REF987654",
    "note": "Resubmitting with the correct bank transfer receipt"
  }
}

docs {
  Edits an offline token payment submission with corrected proof/details —
  either while it's still awaiting review ("pending_verification", e.g.
  the student made a typo and wants to fix it before staff look at it) or
  after it's been rejected ("rejected", the original resubmit-after-
  rejection case). 409 once verification_status is "verified"
  ("This payment has already been verified and can no longer be edited")
  — a finalized payment can't be edited.

  Full re-submission, not a partial patch: every proof field is replaced.
  `amount` is re-validated against the configured token_amount. Same
  conditional requirement as Submit Offline Token Payment: `dd_number`/
  `dd_bank_name`/`dd_date` required for "demand_draft",
  `bank_ref_number` required for "bank_transfer".

  On success: status -> "pending", verification_status ->
  "pending_verification" (a no-op if it was already pending_verification).
  If editing a previously-rejected submission, the prior rejection_reason
  is deliberately left in place until staff make their next decision —
  that's what marks this as a resubmission in the college-admin review
  queue (`isResubmission: true`). Editing a still-pending submission has
  no such flag change since rejection_reason was already null.
}
